    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0694" n="682" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg682"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Prime Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Churchill</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President Roosevelt </hi><anchor
                        n="74" xml:id="d616-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-11">11 May, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>673. Your No. 536.<anchor n="75" xml:id="d616-f2"/> The Chiefs of Staff suggest
                    the amendments contained in the following text. They seem to strengthen our
                    statement.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“From President Eoosevelt and Prime Minister Churchill to Marshal Stalin.</p>
                    <p>In order to give maximum strength to the attack across the sea against
                        northern France, we have transferred part of our landing craft from the
                        Mediterranean to England. This, together with the need for using our
                        Mediterranean land forces in the present Italian battle makes it
                        impracticable to attack the Mediterranean coast of France simultaneously
                        with the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Overlord</hi><anchor n="76"
                            xml:id="d616-f3"/> assault. We are planning to make such an attack
                        later, for which purpose additional landing craft are being sent to the
                        Mediterranean from the United States. In order to keep the greatest number
                        of German forces away from northern France and the eastern front, we are
                        attacking the Germans in Italy at once on a maximum scale and, at the same
                        time, are maintaining a threat against the Mediterranean coast of France.
                        Signed Roosevelt Churchill.[”]</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Prime</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d616-f1" n="74" type="source" xml:id="d616-f1-content">
